---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Base title="How It Works — Metapainting">

  <Hero
    title="How It Works"
    subtitle="The Metapainting method — from completed painting to masked surface to crowd collaboration."
    backgroundImage="/paintings/love-and-burning/PXL_20230218_1.jpg"
    backgroundPosition="center 30%"
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">

      <div class="intro reveal">
        <span class="section-label">The Philosophy</span>
        <p class="font-serif intro__text">
          Metapainting is both a technique and a philosophy. Every piece begins as a finished painting
          by the artist. That painting is then masked, divided into numbered shapes, and opened to the
          crowd. Participants peel off a section, paint their contribution, and become inseparable from
          the work. The result is a layered collaboration — artist and community, structure and freedom,
          all woven together on one surface.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principles reveal">
        <h3 class="font-display principles__title">Core Principles</h3>
        <div class="principles__grid">
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">Divide the Substrate</span>
            <p>Break the surface into distinct regions that give participants clear ownership of their area.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">One Spot Only</span>
            <p>Each person paints one section. This creates genuine individual stakes in a collective outcome.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">Respect Crowd as Medium</span>
            <p>The human is a separate layer with their own variables — prompt, mental state, time, skill, surroundings. Influence is a function.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">Always Be Learning</span>
            <p>Every painting teaches something new. The method evolves with each piece.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- THE 4 PHASES -->
      <div class="phases-overview reveal">
        <span class="section-label font-hand">Step by Step</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">The Four Phases</h2>

        <div class="phase-card card">
          <div class="phase-card__num font-display">01</div>
          <div class="phase-card__content">
            <h3 class="font-display">The Underpainting</h3>
            <p class="font-serif">
              The artist creates a complete, standalone painting on wood or canvas. This forms the
              hidden bottom layer — the structural foundation that will bleed through, underlay, or
              frame the finished collaborative work.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-card card">
          <div class="phase-card__num font-display">02</div>
          <div class="phase-card__content">
            <h3 class="font-display">Precision Masking</h3>
            <p class="font-serif">
              The painting is covered with custom masking tape or laser-cut stencil cutlines.
              The design breaks the surface into numbered polygonal shapes, establishing clear boundaries
              between participant zones.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-card card">
          <div class="phase-card__num font-display">03</div>
          <div class="phase-card__content">
            <h3 class="font-display">Crowd Collaboration</h3>
            <p class="font-serif">
              The painting goes public. Dozens or hundreds of participants each pick one numbered section,
              peel off the masking tape, and paint inside their assigned region. Each person brings their
              own style, color choices, and energy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-card card">
          <div class="phase-card__num font-display">04</div>
          <div class="phase-card__content">
            <h3 class="font-display">Unveiling & Residual Reverberation</h3>
            <p class="font-serif">
              All remaining tape is removed. The sharp, masked lines separate the individual contributions,
              creating a startling synthesis of individual freedom and overall structure. Under blacklight,
              phosphorescent pigments expose an entirely hidden UV dimension.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="cta-box card reveal">
        <h3 class="font-display">Ready to Create?</h3>
        <p class="font-serif">
          Download vector templates and masking guides to get started, or commission a guided Metapainting experience.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-box__actions">
          <a href="/templates" class="btn btn--primary">Get Templates</a>
          <a href="/commission" class="btn btn--outline">Commission an Event</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .intro__text {
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .principles {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .principles__title {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .principles__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .principle {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .principle__label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .principle p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .phases-overview {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .phase-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .phase-card__num {
    font-size: 3rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    line-height: 1;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .phase-card__content h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .phase-card__content p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);

  }

  .cta-box {
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-teal);
  }

  .cta-box h3 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cta-box p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 500px;
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
  }

  .cta-box__actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .principles__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .phase-card {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
